{"page":1,"totalPages":3,"perPage":6,"nextPage":2,"html":"<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/molecule-builder.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/molecule-builder.webp\" alt=\"Sulfur hexafluoride in 3D: a yellow sulfur nucleus with six green fluorines at the corners of an octahedron, each inside a transparent shell\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>6 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/molecule-builder\">Building molecules out of two rules</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Drop atoms into a 3D workspace, bond them together, and watch the geometry arrange itself. Methane finds its tetrahedron, benzene flattens into a hexagon, and cyclohexane buckles into a chair — from two rules and no table of angles.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Chemistry</li><li>3D</li><li>Javascript</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-lab.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-lab.webp\" alt=\"A Red-Black tree simulation mid-repair, with the rotation being narrated underneath\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>10 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/self-balancing-trees\">Four ways to keep a tree balanced</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A search tree is only fast while it stays short, and there are surprisingly different ways to keep it that way: measure heights, colour nodes, roll dice, or give up on binary altogether. Add and delete values in all four and watch each one repair itself a step at a time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Data Structures</li><li>Balanced Binary Tree</li><li>AVL</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-game.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-game.webp\" alt=\"The tree sequence playground, showing an illegal move with the embedded earlier tree ringed\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>7 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/tree-sequence-game\">The game behind TREE(3)</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Two rules, a handful of coloured dots, and a longest game so vast that with three colours nobody can write the answer down. Build sequences here and let the computer tell you the moment you break the rules.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Mathematics</li><li>Logic</li><li>Trees</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/solar-eclipses.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/solar-eclipses.webp\" alt=\"The solar eclipse app showing an annular eclipse shadow crossing South America\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/solar-eclipses\">Visualizing solar eclipses</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A total eclipse is a cosmic coincidence: a moon that just barely covers the sun. This app lets you move through the Sun, Moon and Earth system and watch the geometry that decides which patch of the planet falls into shadow.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>Visualization</li><li>Astronomy</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/task-board.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/task-board.webp\" alt=\"A kanban board with cards spread across To Do, In Progress and Done\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/task-management\">Task management app</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A lightweight, visual task board that runs entirely in the browser. Move work between columns, track what is in flight, and keep day-to-day planning low friction: no backend, no account, nothing to sync.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>React</li><li>Productivity</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/balanced-tree.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/balanced-tree.webp\" alt=\"A balanced binary tree built from twelve values, each node labelled with its height\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-04-09T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.04.09</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/balanced-tree\">Balanced binary tree animated</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Balanced binary trees promise fast inserts, finds and deletes, and rotations are what keep the promise: they stop the tree from growing lopsided. Add and remove nodes here and watch each rotation play out one step at a time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>CSS</li><li>Balanced Binary Tree</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>"}